  <ThingDef ParentName="HelghastArmorMachineableBase">
    <defName>Apparel_HG_Hazopsuit</defName>
    <label>Gunstellig-Compact 'Haz-op' Level A Clean-Suit</label>
    <description>A civilian grade clean suit used by engineers and scientists of the Guntellig-Compact, now disseminated to a wide variety of military contractors across the helghan diaspora, the clean suit has been optimized for ensuring survival in just about any climate or conditions imaginable. Hazmat cleanup teams, petruscite workers, orbital construction and deepcore miners all utilize this apparel to keep them safe. During wartime, many of these civilians are called up to serve in rear-echelon positions, and when they can, they prefer to wear suits like this. Because of the realities of the war, simple aramid plates have been inserted in some of the bulky free space across the suit, but it is by no means intended to be suitable for frontline combat.\n\nThe Compact's idea behind the creation of the Level-A suit was to focus on layers of redundancy, users were expected to wear multiple layers of protection underneath the sturdy exterior rubber, so that in the event of a suit breach the chance of survival was higher then competing products. This level of care was needed for the extremely dangerous work of navigating petruscite extraction sites or assembling helghan space craft in high orbit. It's also kept this suit relevant for decades. Thought it was not originally intended to be used as a space suit, it can be made void ready with minimal preparation.</description>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <unfinishedThingDef>UnfinishedMetallicTechArmor</unfinishedThingDef>
      <researchPrerequisite>FlakArmor</researchPrerequisite>
      <skillRequirements>
        <Crafting>6</Crafting>
      </skillRequirements>
      <recipeUsers Inherit="False">
        <li>HG_Foundry</li>
      </recipeUsers>
	  <displayPriority>202</displayPriority>
    </recipeMaker>
    <graphicData>
