  <ThingDef ParentName="HelghastArmorMachineableBase">
    <defName>Apparel_HG_Hazard</defName>
    <label>Visari Corporation Mk IX Hazard Armor</label>
    <description>Stahl Arms maintained a budget for private arms development independent of the whims of the Helghan state, and from that reserve came the so-called 'Hazmat Troopers'. Designed to withstand exposure to raw unrefined petruscite, radiation, extreme temperatures, and void conditions, the Mark IX was never really meant for large scale production, but rather to outfit a personal cadre of elite guards, not dissimilar to the third shock army's tendency to secure navy equipment to outfit its praetorians. Ostensibly Hazmat troops were paramilitary contractors subservient to the state, but most understood them to be the picked guards of the corporate warlord's personal army. In the fallout of the Petruscide, these suits achieved limited production runs in other states, but the armor proved to be slow, time consuming to make, and heavy, causing it to never achieve mass adoption by any users. Later helghan armor systems would go on to achieve similar performance without these hurdles, yet still, they remain an effective choice for discerning units worried about exposure to the elements.</description>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <unfinishedThingDef>UnfinishedTechArmor</unfinishedThingDef>
      <researchPrerequisite>PoweredArmor</researchPrerequisite>
      <skillRequirements>
        <Crafting>7</Crafting>
      </skillRequirements>
